  Healers can multifire daggers at skilled.  Multifire lets you do more
damage per turn.  That's critical for melee-range combat.  But the great
beauty of missile weapons is that they can be used at much greater
ranges.  

  What's important is hitting the monster with all your missiles before
it reaches melee range.  It doesn't matter as much if it takes 4 turns
or 2.


>A bit much work for any other class.

  The real problem with vanishing missiles is that preservation requires
   - high luck, 
   - a luckstone
   - blessing the missiles
   - enchanting the missiles.  

  It's all or nothing.  Those are difficult to come by early on,
especially all together.

  The main lesson to learn is not to #enhance darts early on, as you
probably won't be able to use them for very long.  In fact the better
your skill the faster you will lose them.

  Non-blessed +0 vanishing missiles (e.g. darts) have a 1/3 chance of
surviving a hit.  That's a 90% chance of vanishing after two hits.  20
starting darts will go down to 2 after you've used them twice.

  +2 darts have a 75% chance of survival after one hit, 50% after two.
Tourists starting with 40 +2 darts will have: 

                                            Total hits
   30 after using them all once   = 40 hits     40
   23 after using them all twice  = 30 hits     70
   17 after using them all thrice = 23 hits     93
   13 after using them all 4x     = 17 hits    100

  That's not completely terrible, but it's also not a viable long term,
or even midterm, strategy.  So #enhancement doesn't seem like a good
idea.  (NB: Tourists can start with as few as 21 darts.  That would take
away the first two rows of that chart.  That's 70 fewer hits by the time
you're down to 13 darts.  Just 30 hits total by then.)

  Can this be overcome early by hard work?  Not really.  #untrapping
dart traps risks deadly poison and will probably get +0 darts with a
miserable 1/3 chance of survival.  A potion of holy water, a luckstone,
and a co-aligned altar will be necessary on DL:1 to stop the bleeding
before it starts.

